  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want the reader's \"⋯\" menu to show page numbers (\"Page 1\", \"Page 1126\") instead of \"Première page\" / \"Dernière page\", and the topic search entry, so that I see where each item leads at a glance.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (validated legacy parity, ROADMAP). Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-11, side-by-side simulator captures 09 (pseudos redacted, attached below when available).\n\n### Observed (2026-11-11, logged out)\n- Legacy: Rechercher | Page 1, Page …, Page 1124, Page 1125, Page 1126, Dernier post.\n- SwiftHFR: Filtrer les posts | Première page, Aller à la page…, Page 1124, Page 1125, Dernière page, Dernier post | Enregistrer cette page hors ligne.\n\n### Scope\n- \"Première page\" → \"Page 1\"; \"Dernière page\" → \"Page <last>\". Keep \"Page …\" and \"Dernier post\" (the operator finds \"Dernière page\" next to \"Dernier post\" confusing).\n- **Keep \"Filtrer les posts\"** here (operator: wanted, good for quick reading).\n- **Search**: the entry exists (LOT-113) but is hidden logged out because the search needs the account's `hash_check` (`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Search/ReaderSearchFlow.swift:10, 20-27`). Check it shows once logged in. If HFR refuses a logged-out search, show the entry with a sign-in prompt rather than hiding it (to decide).\n- \"Enregistrer cette page hors ligne\": removed by N6.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Menu order and labels as above, logged in and out.\n- [ ] Search reachable from the menu when logged in.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
